From f434d95c0f078ca54a8c3a25b51d30c665b4dd70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 18:52:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rc, rtrafd: boot and idle efficiency items from the
 2026-09-20 measurements

Warden's boot-time apply is deferred until a firewall build has happened
(tmpfs marker /tmp/.reaper_firewall_built, written by start_firewall()'s
Reaper block and by a completed apply.sh). The synchronous run inside
start_services was ~6 s of pid 1 on the path to start_wan, and the WAN-up
start_firewall() deleted those chains and re-ran the same script ~15 s
later, so it protected nothing. Enabling Warden from the page after boot
still arms at once (the marker exists by then); a box that never gets a
WAN is armed by rwatch's missing-chain heal, which now says so instead of
reporting a fault.

wanduck: restart_autowan is rate-limited to once a minute while the WAN is
CONNECTED. Every other state keeps the 5 s cadence, and dual WAN never
reaches the branch. The unconditional respawn was about half of what an
idle RT-BE96U burned in init (owner's test: 72 -> 38 cs per 15 s with
wanduck stopped).

rtrafd: rt_bound()'s watcher reaps its own sleep and the main shell reaps
the watcher, so a fast query no longer strands a `sleep 3` on pid 1 (seven
per 4 s class poll: the other half of the init burn). Harness under busybox
ash: a 50 ms command returns in 52 ms with nothing left behind; a hung
single command is still killed at the cap.

Boot waits that guarded observable conditions: the two `sleep 3` around
the /data mount and bcm_knvram become polls (a mount point, then the wlcsm
netlink family the module registers - /proc is not mounted yet there, and
bcm_knvram's init has no deferred work); start_hotplug2's sleep(1) becomes
a poll for its uevent netlink socket; start_dhd_monitor pays its 300 ms
only when a previous debug_monitor exists.

Not done, consumers found at the moment of change: netool (the Network
Analysis and Netstat pages are installed), sysstate (the feedback page
reads its logs), dns_dpi_check (Bandwidth Monitor is reachable through
dns_dpi in rc_support and starts dnsqd). The backlog entry is corrected at
the cut.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
